WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.328
SPEED makes three main contributions.

00:00:02.408 --> 00:00:05.842
First, it introduces spatial-agnostic epitomic tokens,

00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:10.268
a shared dictionary of tokens reused by every
synthetic image patch,

00:00:10.348 --> 00:00:16.256
together with sparse coding matrices that select
only the most significant tokens per image.

00:00:16.336 --> 00:00:19.380
Second, it proposes a feature-recurrent network,

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:25.497
a compact transformer-style network that
recurrently assembles those tokens into hierarchical,

00:00:25.577 --> 00:00:30.704
high-resolution synthetic images while reusing the
same shared tokens and codes.

00:00:30.784 --> 00:00:36.040
Third, it shows this parameterization is a drop-in
module: it plugs into gradient,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.247
distribution, and trajectory matching objectives
alike and improves all of them.

00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:47.560
The framework sets new state-of-the-art results and
is especially strong on high-resolution data.
